---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Industrial Standards Lookup — HowSpec by HowNote"
  description="Browse HowNote standard pages with official metadata, manufacturer references and calculated values clearly separated."
>
  <section class="hero container">
    <div class="eyebrow">HowSpec · Standards</div>
    <h1>Standards with the evidence kept visible.</h1>
    <p>The MVP starts with one pipe-dimension standard and a small, cross-checked size subset. HowNote expands only when the source and relationship type can be displayed clearly.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="container grid">
    <article class="card featured-card">
      <div class="badge-row">
        <span class="badge badge-official">OFFICIAL metadata</span>
        <span class="badge">Pipe / Tube</span>
      </div>
      <h2>ASME B36.10-2022</h2>
      <p class="muted">Welded and Seamless Wrought Steel Pipe. The first dimension-standard reference used by HowNote’s pipe tools.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/standards/asme-b36-10">View standard page →</a>
    </article>

    <article class="card">
      <div class="eyebrow">Evidence type</div>
      <h2>Manufacturer cross-check</h2>
      <p class="muted">A limited set of OD, wall and nominal-mass values is checked across manufacturer publications and labeled separately from official standard metadata.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/sizes">View current size subset →</a>
    </article>

    <article class="card">
      <div class="eyebrow">Evidence type</div>
      <h2>Calculated value</h2>
      <p class="muted">Inside diameter, area and theoretical mass are generated from visible inputs and formulas rather than presented as official standard values.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/tools/pipe-weight-calculator">Open calculator →</a>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="container related-section">
    <div class="card">
      <h2>Planned HowSpec relationship types</h2>
      <p class="muted">Future comparison pages will distinguish identical, modified, not-equivalent, official cross-reference, superseding, related and AI-similar relationships. No unverified “KS = GB” style equivalence will be published.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
